WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.167
-Here at "The Tonight Show," we love songs,

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.567
and we especially love songs written by our audience members

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.667
in an under an hour.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:10.100
It is time for "Battle of the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.234
Here we go.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.868
-♪ Sometimes I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:19.234
♪ And I'm writing a song about another song ♪

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:21.667
-Welcome to "Battle of the Instant Songwriters."

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.868
Before the show, we went through our great talented audience

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:27.834
and we picked out two people who said they were musicians

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:31.934
and we gave them each a made-up song title then asked them --

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.167
We gave them an hour to write

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.167
an original song based on that title.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.634
This is real. Here's a shot of them

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.667
practicing backstage a minute ago.

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:41.133
Yeah. I can't wait to see what they come up with.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.267
So let's meet them right now. Come on over, guys.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.667
Come on. Hi.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.334
Good to see you. Pleasure.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:49.467
Hi. Nice to see you. Thank you for being here.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:52.067
Welcome to the show.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.734
Let's start with contestant number one.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.234
What is your name and where are you from?

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:57.300
-I'm Gemma Laurence and I'm from Brunswick, Maine.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.801
-Hey! We love Maine! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.968
Shout-out to Maine. Oh, I love it.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:05.601
Now, what was the title of the song that you were given?

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.801
-"Is It Love or Is It Cake?"

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:10.534
-Wow. Very topical. I love that.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.534
And what instrument will you be playing?

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.734
Is it the banjo?

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.400
-I'll be playing banjo, yeah. -I love that.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.701
-Reall-- Yeah? -Yeah, I do love banjo.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:17.767
-Yeah?

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.033
-Is that a big instrument in Maine?

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.601
-I think so. People tell me that.

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.300
I come to New York, and they're like, "You're banjo girl!"

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.634
And I'm like, "Okay?"

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.767
-Yeah. Sure, yeah. Why not? I think it's great.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.300
I miss -- I want to hear more banjo.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.400
Yeah, please. -Great.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.133
-Go get settled. Yeah, I love it.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.434
Oh, this is exciting.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:35.901
Okay.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.834
And now, ladies and gentlemen, here to perform

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.901
the world premiere of the soon-to-be classic

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:42.767
"Is It Love or Is It Cake?",

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.367
it's Gemma Laurence.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.167
♪♪

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.701
-♪ Met a girl at the bakery today ♪

00:01:57.634 --> 00:02:01.534
♪ Her eyes inviting me to take a plate ♪

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.501
♪ And I couldn't help ♪

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:09.300
♪ But come back the very next day ♪

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:13.734
♪ Is it love ♪

00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:15.467
♪ Or is it cake? ♪

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:21.267
♪ Saw it for the first time through the glass ♪

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:27.033
♪ Oh, I could see she'd be a total snack ♪

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.734
♪ Unlike a Kit Kat ♪

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:35.367
♪ She won't give my mind a break ♪

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:39.067
♪ Is this love ♪

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:41.334
♪ Or is it just cake? ♪

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:46.400
♪ Could I be disillusioned? ♪

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.701
♪ Without her, I'm a soggy Fig Newton ♪

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:53.200
♪ Do I want her ♪

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.501
♪ Or do I just crave gluten? ♪

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.000
-[ Laughs ] I like that!

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.367
That curveball at the end. I love that.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:08.634
Gemma Laurence, everybody! Give it up for Gemma Laurence!

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.834
Nice curveball at the end. Alright.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.300
Let's meet contestant number two.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.801
What is your name and where are you from?

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.801
-I'm Franklin Rankin from Long Island.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.601
-Franklin Rankin from Long Island.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:20.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.534
Franklin Rankin. Great name.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.968
Franklin, tell everyone, please, what your song title is.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.300
-"Can Elon Musk Buy Me Something?"

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:32.200
-"Can Elon Musk Buy Me Something?"

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.300
Yeah. He's watching the show tonight.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.701
So, yeah, if it's good, yeah, Elon could probably get --

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.033
take care of something.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.300
What instrument will you be playing tonight?

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.834
-Guitar. -Guitar!

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.334
Alright. Perfect.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.701
Fantastic. I love guitar, too.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:47.000
Franklin, whenever -- Get ready. Whenever you get settled.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.801
♪♪

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:52.067
"Can Elon Musk Buy Me Something?" Okay.

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.434
Ladies and gentlemen, get ready for the world premiere

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.534
of "Can Elon Musk Buy Me Something?"

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.100
by Franklin Rankin.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.033
♪♪

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.701
-♪ I know he just bought Twitter ♪

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.734
♪ And it probably cost a lot ♪

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.067
♪ But summer's coming up ♪

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:15.334
♪ And my account's not looking hot ♪

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.934
♪ So maybe just a Tesla ♪

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:20.300
♪ Or a glossy diamond ring ♪

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.200
♪ Oh, can Elon Musk buy me something? ♪

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:28.267
♪ I'd even take a rocket ♪

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.901
♪ Or a little bit of Doge ♪

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.834
♪ A trip to Turks and Caicos ♪

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:36.968
♪ Or a gift card to Lowe's ♪

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.567
♪ When SpaceX hits the moon ♪

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:41.234
♪ Maybe he'll take me for a ride ♪

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:44.734
♪ Oh, can Elon Musk buy me something? ♪

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:48.601
♪ Wouldn't mind a Peloton ♪

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.300
♪ 'Cause I'm working on my core ♪

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.901
♪ He can hit me up on Venmo ♪

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.767
♪ At FranklinRankin4 ♪

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.033
♪ If you're running out of pesos ♪

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:02.334
♪ You can borrow from Jeff Bezos ♪

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:05.067
♪ Oh, can Elon Musk buy me ♪

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.400
♪ If you're watching, please buy me ♪

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:10.300
♪ Can Elon Musk buy me something? ♪

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:15.501
-Nice Bezos line!

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.667
Nice Bezos line right there.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.634
Franklin, thank you very much.

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.434
Franklin Rankin.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:24.234
Now it is time to see who won.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:26.601
And we're gonna let our great audience decide the winner.

00:05:26.601 --> 00:05:27.701
Is it...

00:05:27.701 --> 00:05:28.834
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:30.067
...Gemma Laurence?

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:35.334
Or is it Franklin Rankin?

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.734
Looks like the winner is Gemma Laurence!

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.400
Gemma, congratulations!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.901
You are the winner

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:43.934
of "Battle of the Instant Songwriters."

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:47.801
You will be going home with, of course, a sweatshirt

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.467
that says "I Love Music."

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:51.167
-Yes! -Congratulations.

00:05:51.167 --> 00:05:53.400
You really deserve it, and you earned it. Yeah.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:58.501
Oh, also, you're going home with a Samsung Galaxy 2 Pro.

00:05:58.501 --> 00:05:59.801
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:05.567
A Galaxy Book2 Pro to write and record songs on.

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:07.167
That is for you. Congratulations.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:08.534
-Thank you so much. -Franklin...

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.067
I'm sorry. [ Laughter ]

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.701
But I'm glad you came.

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:16.968
No, I'm just kidding. We have a sweatshirt.

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:18.334
We have a sweatshirt. -Aw, sick.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:19.667
-Yeah, it says "I Love Music."

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:21.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:23.801
That's great. That's your size? It fits perfect.

00:06:23.801 --> 00:06:25.534
Alright. We'll be right b-- I'm kidding.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:28.601
And a Samsung Galaxy Pro.

00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:30.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:32.300
Write, record, make an album, bud.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.901
Make an album, pal.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:36.300
Give it up for our two new instant songwriters.

